I walk over to the register.
A young man stands behind the counter.
He is a barista in the café.
I smile at him.
He nods warmly.
"Hi," he says.
"What would you like?" he asks.
"Hi," I answer.
"I would like a black coffee, please."
"And may I also ask for a cinnamon roll?"
"Of course," he says.
"A black coffee and a cinnamon roll."
"Would you like to sit here?" he asks.
"Yes please, I will sit down over there," I say.
"Alright," the barista says.
"I will make your coffee now."
"Thank you very much," I say.
